# core/.preserve — the ONE definition of which core/ files survive an upgrade.
#
# Read by all four deploy paths: install.sh, install.ps1,
# cli/commands/init.js and cli/commands/upgrade.js (both via syncCore() in
# cli/commands/sync-assets.js). If you add a path here it is honoured
# everywhere; there is deliberately no second list.
#
# SEMANTICS — skip-if-exists:
#   destination has the file  -> leave it exactly as-is, never overwrite
#   destination does not      -> seed it from the repo copy
# That single rule is both first-install seeding and upgrade preservation.
# There is no merge: merging would need per-file format knowledge, and a
# wrong merge loses rows just as surely as an overwrite does.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE — files the RUNNING SYSTEM writes rows into at their
# installed path. Not "files that look like state": something shipped in this
# repo must actually instruct an agent to write to it. Grep before adding.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE — shipped content. Listing a template freezes
# every existing install on the version it happens to have; users would stop
# receiving new agent routes, new lessons and new tier definitions forever.
# That is a real cost, not a safe default. `memory/agency-dispatch.md`,
# `memory/autonomy-tiers.json` and `memory/lessons/*.md` are read-only at
# runtime and are deliberately absent from this list.
#
# FORMAT: one path per line, relative to core/, forward slashes, exact file
# paths only (no globs, no directories). `#` starts a comment.
# .github/scripts/check-core-preserve.js fails the build if a path listed
# here does not exist in the repo — a typo here preserves nothing, silently.

# Legacy copy of the Active Projects registry. The live registry is
# {agency-root}/memory/medium-term.md (what /recall and /pd-resume read, and what
# `agency new` and project-scaffolder write); the installers seed it from THIS
# file only when it is absent. Older installs accumulated their rows here (that is
# where project-scaffolder used to write), so it must survive an upgrade to be
# carried over once. Losing it would lose those rows.
memory/medium-term.md

# Delegator route cache. CLAUDE.md instructs every caller to append the
# resolved (task-pattern -> route) pair here on a cache miss.
memory/delegator-cache.md

# NOTE: quality-prefs.md used to be listed here as a shipped seed under
# core/memory/. It is user data, not shipped content — the canonical copy now
# lives at {agency-root}/memory/quality-prefs.md (the operator's runtime
# memory dir, never touched by core/ sync), created on first write by
# skills/quality-loop-router/SKILL.md. It does not belong in this list: this
# list only covers files that ship a seed copy under core/ AND get written to
# at their installed path (see the "skip-if-exists" semantics above) — with no
# repo copy under core/, there is nothing to seed or preserve here, and
# .github/scripts/check-core-preserve.js fails the build on any listed path
# that doesn't exist under core/, so a dangling entry is actively wrong, not
# just harmless.
